WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.140
Is your nervous system built of separate cells, like liver or skin?

2
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.760
Or is it one continuous network of fused fibres?

3
00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.100
There were two answers.

4
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.180
The neuron theory said each nerve cell is a separate cell, bounded by its own

5
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.180
membrane.

6
00:00:19.633 --> 00:00:24.193
The reticular theory said the fine branches fuse into one continuous net.

7
00:00:25.183 --> 00:00:27.643
It comes down to the point where two branches meet.

8
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:32.143
Does one membrane run on, or do two face each other across a gap?

9
00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:35.343
Here is the one idea to carry through.

10
00:00:35.343 --> 00:00:37.303
A touch is not a fusion.

11
00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:42.903
Whether two touching branches are one cell or two depends on the membrane where they

12
00:00:42.903 --> 00:00:48.543
meet. Settling it takes evidence that bears directly on that membrane: seeing it, or

13
00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:49.783
testing what crosses it.

14
00:00:50.667 --> 00:00:55.747
Under the best light microscope, two points closer than about 200 nanometres blur

15
00:00:55.747 --> 00:00:56.747
into one.

16
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.440
The gap at a chemical synapse is about 20 nanometres.

17
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.240
That is about ten times below the limit.

18
00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:09.980
Depth is worse. Two branches close together, one above the other, can look like one

19
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.340
line as you focus through.

20
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:17.110
Picture one contact under the best light microscope of the 1890s.

21
00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:19.230
What does each theory predict you will see?

22
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:30.943
The same thing. Two facing membranes and a fused junction give the same smudge.

23
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:40.470
So the evidence had to come from elsewhere: from whole cells, from embryos, and from

24
00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:41.790
the direction signals travel.

25
00:01:42.883 --> 00:01:46.443
The answer, for the vertebrate nervous system, is separate cells.

26
00:01:47.303 --> 00:01:50.583
They pass signals across specialized contacts, called synapses.

27
00:01:51.717 --> 00:01:53.837
That is why this matters for development.

28
00:01:54.757 --> 00:01:58.777
In vertebrates, development has to wire separate cells to the right partners.

29
00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.210
A touch is not a fusion.

30
00:02:02.110 --> 00:02:03.630
The difference lies at the membrane.
